      "Model, not measurement: every number follows from the spec's parameters.",
      "Link: frames are serialized at link_bps with preamble, FCS, padding and inter-frame gap; each slave forwards with a fixed delay; frame loss (if configured) happens before the first slave.",
      "ESC: mailboxes are 1-buffer SyncManagers; a write is accepted only while \"mailbox out\" is empty, a read returns data only while \"mailbox in\" is full. Process data uses 3-buffer SyncManagers: the application reads the newest outputs when its PDI is free.",
      "PDI: the slave application moves mailbox data (the whole SyncManager buffer, or only the message plus the triggering last byte, per pdi.mailbox_access) and process data at the configured rate plus a fixed overhead per access, one access at a time; mailbox and process data compete for it.",
      "Master: cycle-driven; it learns whether a mailbox write was accepted from the returning working counter and retries otherwise; master CPU and operating-system delays are not modelled beyond the configured cycle jitter.",
      "EoE carries UDP/IPv4 datagrams: a simplified tunnel without TCP, ARP or IP fragmentation.",
      "Payload bytes are generated deterministically and checked byte for byte and by SHA-256 at the receiver.",
      "Ethernet reference: TCP over a dedicated link at the same rate, MSS 1460 in 1538 wire bytes per segment, steady state, no loss, no slow start; a lower bound on plain-Ethernet time, not a prediction."
